1.3 We offer the Software only if you accept. There is no use outside this Agreement.

1.4 You agree that electronic acceptance is the same as a signature under the United States Electronic Signatures in Global and National Commerce Act (E-SIGN), 15 U.S.C. section 7001 and following, the Uniform Electronic Transactions Act, and similar laws. You consent to receive this Agreement, receipts, and legal notices in electronic form.


2. WHO THIS BINDS

2.1 You must be at least 18 years old, or the age of legal majority where you live, whichever is higher. The Software and the Website are not directed to children under 13. You must not let a child under 13 use them or send us a child's personal information. If you are under 18, do not accept this Agreement.

2.2 If you use the Software for a company or other organization, you represent that you can bind it. "You" then includes that organization. If you lack authority, you must not accept. If you use the Software anyway, you accept personally.

2.3 You may not accept this Agreement, buy a subscription, or use the Software if you are barred under export and sanctions law, or if a court or government order prohibits you from doing so.

2.4 This Agreement gives you a copyright license. It is not a sale of goods except to the extent a mandatory consumer law treats digital content as goods. Title to the Software does not pass to you.


3. DEFINITIONS

"Analysis" means the OCR text, screenshot evidence, and classification result (including Safe, Suspicious, Phishing, Unsure, or similar labels) produced when Securely examines screen content.

"Computer" means a Windows device on which you install and run Securely.

"Input" means screen pixels, OCR text, settings, the email you use for Stripe, and other data the Software processes on your Computer or sends to Securely servers you invoke.

"Paid subscription" means an active Stripe subscription for Securely that Delexoo honors for the email you activate in the app.

"Stripe" means Stripe, Inc. and its affiliates, which process payment.

"Website" means trysecurely.com, trysecurely.vercel.app, and the pages Delexoo serves for Securely, including terms, privacy, billing, releases, and this Agreement.


4. WHAT SECURELY IS

4.1 Securely is a Windows overlay that can capture the primary display, run OCR, and send evidence to a server-side analysis service so you can see Safe / Warning / Phishing style status on the widget. It includes a floating dashboard for monitoring settings, billing activation, audit history, and release notes.

4.2 Securely is a decision aid. It is not a full antivirus product, not a firewall, not identity theft insurance, and not a promise that every phishing page, scam, or malicious UI will be detected. False negatives and false positives can occur.

4.3 A paid subscription is a limited copyright license to use the Software while the subscription remains active. It is not a sale of our intellectual property and not an assignment of any right except the limited rights in section 5.

4.4 Features can differ by version, by Windows build, by network availability, and by whether this Computer has an active paid subscription. Descriptions on the Website, in a demo, in a video, or in a conversation explain the product in ordinary language. They are not a warranty or a service-level agreement.

4.5 The price of Securely is three United States dollars per month, renewing until canceled, unless a promotional code changes the amount Stripe charges. Taxes may be added. Cancel anytime through the Stripe customer portal linked from the app or Website.

4.6 The Software requires a supported Windows 10 or Windows 11 install and the Microsoft Edge WebView2 runtime. You are responsible for installing system software the version you use requires.

4.7 Continuous (24/7) monitoring requires your explicit consent in the product. You are responsible for complying with workplace, school, and local privacy rules before leaving monitoring on.


